Basic Verilog Module Structure:
```verilog
module gate_level_circuit (input wire a, b, c, output wire f);
    wire w1, w2;
    and G1 (w1, a, b);
    not G2 (w2, c);
    or  G3 (f, w1, w2);
endmodule
```

Structural Verilog Design Hierarchy:
- Top-level modules instantiate lower-level submodules, connecting their ports via internal wires:
```verilog
module full_adder (input wire a, b, cin, output wire sum, cout);
    wire s1, c1, c2;
    half_adder ha1 (.a(a), .b(b), .sum(s1), .cout(c1));
    half_adder ha2 (.a(s1), .b(cin), .sum(sum), .cout(c2));
    or g1 (cout, c1, c2);
endmodule
```
